        { term: 'Quant', definition: 'Short for "quantitative analyst", someone who uses math and programming to build trading strategies and financial models.', example: 'Jim Simons hired mathematicians and physicists, not Wall Street bankers, to build his fund\'s trading system, because he believed math skills mattered more than finance knowledge.' },
        { term: 'Data-Driven', definition: 'Making decisions based on measurable evidence and statistical analysis rather than opinions, hunches, or emotions.', example: 'Instead of saying "I think tech stocks will go up," a data-driven approach would be: "Tech stocks have risen in 72% of quarters when interest rates fell, and rates are falling now."' }
