        { term: 'Kelly Criterion', definition: 'A formula for calculating the optimal bet size to maximize long-term wealth growth: Kelly % = (bp - q) / b, where b = odds, p = win probability, q = loss probability.', example: 'If you have a 60% chance of winning even money (b=1): Kelly = (1×0.6 - 0.4) / 1 = 20% of bankroll per bet.' }
