        'The Exponential Moving Average (EMA) gives more weight to recent data points, making it more responsive to new information. While a 50-day SMA weights all 50 days equally, a 50-day EMA might give 40% of its weight to the last 10 days. This responsiveness is crucial in fast-moving markets where old data quickly becomes irrelevant.',
