          explanation: 'The random walk hypothesis is a useful approximation but not literally true. Decades of academic research (Jegadeesh & Titman 1993, Fama & French 1988) show persistent time series patterns in returns. These patterns are small, typically 1-3% annualized alpha, but at scale with leverage and thousands of trades, they generate enormous profits for quant funds.'
