        { term: 'Risk Parity', definition: 'A portfolio construction method where each asset class contributes equally to total portfolio risk, rather than allocating equal dollar amounts. This typically leads to higher bond and lower equity weights than traditional portfolios.', example: 'Bridgewater\'s All Weather fund uses risk parity: bonds get higher weight because they\'re less volatile, so each asset class contributes ~25% to total risk.' }
