      { term: 'Z-Score', definition: 'The number of standard deviations a spread is from its mean, the primary signal for entry/exit.', example: 'A z-score of +2.5 means the spread is 2.5σ above the mean, strong sell signal', sentence: 'The model entered the trade when the _____ exceeded 2.0 and exited when it crossed zero.' },
      { term: 'Half-Life', definition: 'The expected time for a mean-reverting spread to return halfway to its mean from its current level.', example: 'A 10-day half-life means the spread halves its deviation every 10 trading days', sentence: 'With a _____ of only 5 days, this pair offered rapid convergence and quick profit realization.' }
