          explanation: 'The 1987 crash saw the S&P 500 drop 20.5% in one day, a 20+ sigma event under GBM that should occur once in billions of universe lifetimes. Real markets have much fatter tails than GBM predicts, which is why volatility smiles exist and why risk management based purely on GBM is dangerous.'
