          explanation: 'The VRP exists because option sellers bear crash risk, occasional massive losses. Option buyers pay a premium (higher IV) for insurance against these tail events. On average, selling options at implied vol and hedging at realized vol is profitable, but the occasional Volmageddon can wipe out years of premiums.'
