      { term: 'Leverage Effect', definition: 'The empirical asymmetry where falling prices increase volatility more than rising prices. Named for the mechanical increase in financial leverage when equity values decline.', example: 'A 5% S&P 500 drop typically raises the VIX by 4-5 points. A 5% rally typically lowers the VIX by only 1-2 points.', sentence: 'The leverage effect creates the volatility skew in equity options, OTM puts are expensive because crashes both increase vol and move the strike closer to the money.' }
