          explanation: 'The hype around AI/deep learning in finance vastly exceeds reality. In Kaggle competitions, industry research, and actual trading performance, gradient boosting with good features consistently beats neural networks for tabular financial data. The signal-to-noise ratio is simply too low for deep learning to exploit without overfitting. The exceptions (NLP, order flow) have much more data and higher signal-to-noise.'
