          explanation: 'Before 2000, there was no high-frequency trading, minimal ETF impact, and different market microstructure. Training models on this data can teach patterns that no longer exist. The best quant ML systems use adaptive windows, giving more weight to recent data while retaining enough history to learn robust relationships. Quality, relevance, and recency trump raw volume.'
