        'VWAP (Volume-Weighted Average Price) algorithms distribute execution proportional to historical volume patterns. Since volume is U-shaped (high at open and close, low mid-day), VWAP trades more at the open and close. VWAP is ideal for patient, benchmark-tracking orders. It minimizes market impact by blending with natural volume. Limitation: it\'s predictable, predatory algorithms can detect VWAP execution patterns and front-run them.',
        'TWAP (Time-Weighted Average Price) distributes execution evenly across time regardless of volume. TWAP is less predictable than VWAP (since it doesn\'t follow the volume curve) but may have higher impact during low-volume periods. TWAP is preferred when the priority is unpredictability and information leakage is a concern, for example, when trading ahead of a catalyst.',
