          explanation: 'When Robinhood offers "free trading," the cost is hidden in the spread. Robinhood sells order flow to Citadel Securities and Virtu, who execute at prices slightly worse than the best available. On a $10,000 trade with a 5 bps cost, you\'re paying $5, hidden in the execution price rather than an explicit commission. For large institutional orders, implicit costs (impact, spread) dwarf any commission savings.'
