      'Risk-neutral pricing is the crown jewel of quantitative finance, an elegant framework that prices any derivative as a discounted Q-expectation without needing to estimate risk premia or investor preferences. But its power comes from assumptions: no arbitrage, continuous hedging, liquid markets, and known dynamics. The best quants master both the framework AND its limitations. They use risk-neutral pricing daily for the $640 trillion derivatives market, while maintaining deep awareness of when the assumptions can fail, because those failures are exactly when the largest losses occur.'
