      'Zero tail dependence (λ_L = λ_U = 0) means: lim P(Y < F⁻¹(u) | X < F⁻¹(u)) → 0 as u → 0. In plain English: if you know one variable is in its extreme tail, the probability of the other also being extreme approaches the unconditional probability. For credit risk, this means the model predicts that even during a severe crisis with many defaults, remaining borrowers are not at elevated risk. The 2008 crisis proved this catastrophically wrong.'
