      { takeaway: 'Bayesian shrinkage and model averaging produce more robust estimates than pure frequentist methods', detail: 'Shrinkage pulls noisy estimates toward structured priors, reducing estimation error by ~50%. Model averaging hedges against model misspecification by weighting multiple models by evidence. Both techniques are essential when data is limited and parameters are uncertain, the standard financial context.' },
      { takeaway: 'Bayesian regime-switching provides probabilistic market state assessment for adaptive allocation', detail: 'Rather than binary bull/bear signals, Bayesian regime models give posterior probabilities of each state, enabling proportional portfolio responses. As the posterior shifts, positions adjust gradually, avoiding the whipsaw of threshold-based signals while capturing genuine regime changes.' }
