      'The COVID crash was a real-time exam in quantitative finance. Every concept from this curriculum was tested simultaneously: stochastic calculus (pricing with VIX at 82), risk-neutral pricing (implied vol skew inverted), copulas (universal correlation spike), Bayesian methods (regime detection and adaptation), execution (trading in broken markets), and risk management (surviving 34% in 23 days). The firms that had integrated mastery of all these tools navigated the crisis and captured the recovery. Those with fragmented knowledge suffered. This is why integration matters.'
