          explanation: 'LTCM had two Nobel Prize winners and the best mathematical models on Wall Street. Their models were mathematically correct but ignored the possibility that markets could become so illiquid that hedging was impossible. Market intuition, understanding liquidity, participant behavior, and regime dynamics, is what prevents mathematical models from being applied beyond their valid range.'
