            { label: 'Accept the loss and don\'t change anything, extreme events are unpredictable by definition', consequence: 'Extreme events are not unpredictable, they\'re just unpredictable under the WRONG model. A t-copula with appropriate tail dependency would have assigned material probability to this joint loss event. The lesson of every major quant failure: "unpredictable" events are usually predictable under a better model.', score: 0 }
