            { label: 'Conduct a structured evaluation: (1) map your exact optimization problem to the quantum annealer, (2) compare solution quality and speed vs your classical optimizer on the same problem, (3) if the quantum solution matches quality at genuine speedup, adopt for the overnight batch, but maintain the classical system as backup. Meanwhile, invest in quantum readiness for the full pipeline', consequence: 'Correct. Quantum computing claims require rigorous benchmarking: same problem, same constraints, same quality threshold. If the quantum annealer genuinely solves your specific optimization 100× faster with equivalent solution quality, it\'s a clear win for the overnight batch. But maintain the classical backup (quantum systems can have uptime issues), and invest in quantum readiness for higher-value applications (MC pricing, real-time optimization) when fault-tolerant hardware matures.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Reject, 2 hours overnight is fast enough', consequence: 'While 2 hours is acceptable for overnight rebalancing, the evaluation is about more than this single use case. If quantum truly delivers for optimization, it opens the door to: intraday rebalancing, more complex constraint sets, and larger stock universes. Rejecting without evaluation means missing genuine opportunity.', score: 0 }
